  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "$$\n\\begin{gathered}\ny^2=-8(x-2) \\\\\ny^2=24(x+2) \\cdots(2)\n\\end{gathered}\n$$\nSolving (1) and $(2) \\Rightarrow x=-1$\nArea $=2\\left[\\int_{-2}^{-1} 2 \\sqrt{6} \\sqrt{x+2} \\mathrm{dx}+\\int_{-1}^2 2 \\sqrt{2} \\sqrt{2-x} \\mathrm{dx}\\right]=\\frac{32}{3} \\sqrt{6}$ sq. unit\n<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/wbjee/XbnA7qORB_ifSCmYsFQsd1pGSu1T5AZKUk51DWfKh3U.original.fullsize.png\">",
